description:
Tri Language is a DSL for ternary computing with advanced type system features and dual-target code generation. Key innovations: (1) Linear Types + Ownership (Let/Inout/Sink/Set modes); (2) Algebraic Effects + Handlers with platform-aware resolution; (3) Bit/Trit Pattern Matching at hardware level; (4) Content-Addressed Functions via SHA256 AST hashing; (5) Result Type (Austral-style error handling); (6) Array Combinators; (7) Pipe Operator; (8) Dual-Target Codegen (Zig + Verilog). Enables zero-cost abstractions while maintaining memory safety.

**Linear Types Example:**
```
fn consume(let x: Tensor): void { ... }
fn modify(inout x: Tensor): void { ... }
fn destroy(sink x: Tensor): void { ... }
fn create(): Set Tensor { ... }
```

**Algebraic Effects Example:**
```
effect State { fn get(): T, fn set(x: T): void }
fn counter() with State[i32] {
  let n = get(); set(n + 1);
}
```

**Compilation Pipeline:**
```
.tri → AST → Type Check → {Zig codegen, Verilog codegen}
                                    ↓              ↓
                               CPU binary     FPGA bitstream
```
